00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.580
Now, the human impulse to find meaning

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.070
in the stars is nothing new.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.980
Ancient Babylonians were
reading the night sky

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.870
back in the 2nd century BCE.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:57.703
In ancient Greece,

00:02:57.703 --> 00:03:00.150
astrology developed in
tandem with astronomy

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.340
and was treated with respect

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.070
by the likes of Ptolemy and Plato.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.010
Throughout history,

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.680
kings would use court astrologers

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.400
to help them make important decisions

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.780
like who to invade or what
flavor ice cream to eat.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:10.860
In the 12th century,

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.040
astrology became heavily tied to medicine,

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.030
and the job title physician
astrologer was a real thing.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.680
Astrology was even taught at
universities across Europe

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.550
until the late 17th century!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.740
But around then, The Age of Enlightenment,

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.770
coupled with propaganda
and political pressure,

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.560
put a dent in astrology's credibility.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.720
For a couple hundred years,

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.670
it was relegated to a fringe
interest of freaky weirdos.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.600
For a long time, in many places,

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.010
it was even illegal to predict futures.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.770
The spiritualist movement of
the mid-to-late 19th century

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.650
would revive the ancient craft somewhat,

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.490
but it would never be as well-respected.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.140
Fast forward to the swinging '60s,

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.930
and baby boomers zealously
embraced astrology.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:47.900
And to this day, it's remained a huge,

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.160
if hugely mocked, part of our culture.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.340
But how did we get here?

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.110
What accounts for astrology's
enduring popularity?

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:57.010
You can largely thank
occult enthusiast Alan Leo,

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.770
a late 19th century New Ager

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.670
who super liked reading the stars.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.300
But he had a big problem,

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.850
it was still illegal in England

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.240
to predict the future for money.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.810
So, after going to court and
being fined for his lil' hobby,

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.360
he took his lawyer's advice
and stopped making predictions.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.150
But what good was astrology
without predictions of death,

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.730
thunderstorms or unsightly
pimples on your wedding day?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.620
Leo was about to figure it out.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.410
See, he also believed
that the Age of Aquarius

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.500
was fast approaching.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.280
This was going to be a blissful
era of raised consciousness

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.330
and humanity reaching its true potential.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.830
He wanted to help everyone get ready

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.340
for this dope galactic spectacle,

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.700
specifically by achieving
better self-understanding.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.660
Importantly, Leo believed
that character is destiny.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.160
That meant astrology should help people

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.950
better understand their
character and temperament,

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.600
rather than predicting external
happenings like car crashes.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.870
And here's the major plus,

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.210
describing someone's personality

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.200
is not technically telling the future,

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.550
thus it was not illegal.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.240
Now, quick sidebar,
you know your sun sign?

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.080
That's not your whole
astrological picture.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.720
Professional astrologers take into account

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.470
the position of every single
planet in the solar system

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.700
when crafting a star chart.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.630
But that shit is very complicated

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.720
and requires a lot of math and training.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.130
Thus, it was super expensive

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.320
and pretty much exclusive
to the upper class.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.740
This made astrology kind
of hard to popularize.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.550
So Leo came up with the ultimate shortcut,

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.160
teach people their sun sign,

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.200
and draw conclusions about their character

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.720
based solely on that.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.910
This bite-sized approach

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.100
to the craft proved massively popular.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.560
Soon, newspapers would
start publishing horoscopes,

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.780
and life would never be the same

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.620
for any of you two-faced Geminis.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:24.453
Just kidding!

00:05:24.453 --> 00:05:27.280
But yeah, he basically made
abbreviated horoscopes a thing.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.930
Though he couldn't have possibly predicted

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.430
the 21st century meme explosion

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.100
he was effectively setting in motion.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.680
Leo's sun-sign-only approach

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.710
would largely define modern astrology.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.660
Standardizing zodiac signs also,

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.560
helpfully, made astrology
marketable on a massive level

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.650
via cheap almanacs.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.200
Conveniently, this was happening

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.080
just as the consumer capitalist economy

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.320
was entering full swing.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.890
At the same time, Leo
would inspire astrologer

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:51.130
Dane Rudhyar to take this character stuff

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:52.930
a step further in the 1930s

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:56.220
by invoking a sparkly new
type of science: psychology!

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:59.050
Specifically by borrowing
from one Carl Jung.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:01.580
Side note, turns out
Jung was a big ol' weirdo

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.090
who liked alchemy and astrology.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.140
In fact, Jung liked astrology so much

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.290
that it's speculated
his zeal for the craft

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.810
was at least partially responsible

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:11.290
for his famous breakup
with mentor Sigmund Freud!

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:12.710
This makes sense because,

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:15.460
as writers Keiron Le Grace
and Safron Rossi explain

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:16.987
in their book Jung on Astrology,

00:06:16.987 --> 00:06:19.900
"At root, both astrology
and Jungian psychology

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.410
might be seen as being engaged

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.340
with the critical task of
developing greater self-knowledge,

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.630
of bringing to awareness
the unconscious factors

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:28.530
underlying our life experience."

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.728
Rudhyar formally merged astrology
with Jungian psychology,

00:06:31.728 --> 00:06:33.960
especially his notions about
the collective unconscious

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:34.850
and archetypes.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:37.360
Thus, he created "psychological astrology"

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.700
and popularized the idea
of reading your horoscope

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.420
as a cheaper version of seeing a shrink.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.640
Rest assured, not everybody was happy

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.570
about the mainstreaming of astrology.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.780
In 1952, cultural critic and
notorious grump Theodor Adorno

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.170
wrote a semi-aggressive 78-page screed

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.720
critiquing sun-sign columns.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.340
He declared that fans of astrology

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.400
were "persons who do not any longer feel

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.830
that they are the self-determining
subjects of their fate."

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.970
He studied Los Angeles Times horoscopes

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.340
and noted certain themes.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:06.010
Specifically, that they seemed
to promote bourgeois values

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:07.950
like tact, hard work, and success,

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:09.000
while flattering people

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.090
about how intuitive they supposedly were.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:13.470
He wondered how, in the
age of astrophysics,

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.840
anyone could possibly believe

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:17.230
that their personality was
affected by their date of birth.

00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:20.020
That same question
continues to be posed today.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.130
For her part, scholar Kirstine Munk argues

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.120
that two world wars, nuclear weapons,

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:25.560
and the environmental crisis

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.000
have all made science
seem a lot less sexy.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.320
This then leads people to seek out

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.300
decidedly-unscientific
things like astrology.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.350
But what if the popularity of astrology

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.400
in modern times isn't just explainable,

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.620
but was actually pretty inevitable?

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.900
Back in 1966, sociologist Jaques Maitre

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:44.690
argued that astrology is
actually a perfect fit

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.920
for modernity, and many have since agreed.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:49.120
See, as scholar Marshall Berman explained,

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:52.100
rapid change is one of the
central tenets of modernity.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:54.150
Whether it's the decreased
power of religious

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.490
and other social institutions,

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.500
or rapidly increasing globalization,

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.140
our world is in a constant state of flux.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:03.180
As Munk explains, "The world
today seems more enchanted

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.370
than ever, but is also in certain ways

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:06.850
more dangerous and demanding.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:09.480
We are constantly faced with
the challenge to make decisions

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.570
and to act in the world
without full knowledge

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:13.350
and without a privileged point of view."

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.420
Frequent job changes, cross-country moves,

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.460
divorces and so-on add far
more variables to everyday life

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.800
than our ancestors ever had.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.790
Meanwhile, a decaying social fabric

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.330
leaves us all as lone agents,

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:24.970
trying to figure out how to behave.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.440
This creates fraught situations

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.650
where we worry about
making the wrong choices,

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.650
about being the wrong kind of person.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.177
As scholar Olav Hammer writes,

00:08:32.177 --> 00:08:35.310
"In late modernity, we
construct who we really are

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:37.750
by engaging in self-reflexive speculation

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.950
and considering a variety of options."

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:42.000
That's where astrology comes
in for a lot of people:

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.870
as a mediating force
to help them make sure

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:44.870
they're not fucking up.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.360
As Munk puts it, "To
use astrology is a way

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.070
to claim a home in the cosmos."

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.500
That's during a time when a lot of us

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.490
don't have that psychic
home anywhere else.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:54.810
That's why astrology is
particularly attractive

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.710
to people in liminal situations,

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.170
like a breakup or job loss.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.870
In a world full of choices,
the guidance of the stars,

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.760
no matter how unproven, can
feel centering for some.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.750
Munk notes that astrology
both lets us feel "acted upon"

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.600
by forces larger than ourselves

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:09.897
while also helping folks

00:09:09.897 --> 00:09:11.490
"to make a shift of perspective

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:14.570
and to reconstruct their worlds
in slightly different ways."

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.980
Reading your horoscope on
the internet, she explains,

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:19.690
can "magically create a
foreground and background"

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.070
for the "self-reflective
modern individual"

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.500
who might feel ungrounded
in their real life.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.210
In this way, she believes its appeal

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:28.520
is largely about "agency and empowerment."

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.700
Perhaps it's no wonder, then,

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.610
that astrology has, in America,

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.720
traditionally attracted
marginalized groups.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:34.970
Like women and people of color,

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.560
who are all too often
denied power in daily life.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:39.600
Some scholars think
astrology even functions

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.240
as a powerful coping mechanism.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.450
This all makes it somewhat
ironic that astrology

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:46.320
has become an important spiritual
outlet for so many people

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:48.360
precisely because it's so aptly adjusted

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.210
to modern capitalism and mass production.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.800
But the popularity of astrology

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.440
is also reflective of the way
society now sees individuals.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.920
Remember how old-school astrology

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.910
was all about big events like
wars and royal coronations.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.200
Rather than about little old you

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.930
and your inexplicable romantic
affinity for mouth-breathers?

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.210
That's in large part because,

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.740
before the early modern era,

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.970
individualism wasn't all that important.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.300
It was thought that every person

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.850
had a few basic core
characteristics in common.

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:15.060
But the concept of the unique individual

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.890
eventually caught on, with a little help

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:19.400
from Renaissance philosopher
Michel de Montaigne,

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:20.240
among others.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.930
In our late modern times, the
pursuit of that authentic,

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.960
unique self has become paramount.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.830
And astrology is one way of sussing out

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:29.400
and understanding your own
quirks and idiosyncrasies.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.050
In the process, Hammer explains,

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:33.910
we've seen "decreasing
concern with cosmogonic myths

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.330
or social charters and
an increasing insistence

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.740
on personalized legends,
self-centered rituals

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.570
and the spiritual transformation
of each individual."

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.320
The individualization of religion,

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:45.240
of finding salvation in your own self,

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.227
is distinctly modern and
perfectly suited to astrology.

00:10:48.227 --> 00:10:50.010
And this understandably coincides

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:51.540
with the overall reduction in power

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.200
of organized religions in our age.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:54.667
Hammer writes that, these days,

00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:57.280
"Not only is truth to be
found within each of us:

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:00.400
the very locus of
spirituality is our own self."

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:03.900
But what if your own self
is kind of discombobulated?

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.562
How can you make sense of your life?

00:11:05.562 --> 00:11:07.940
Astrology can help with
that too, apparently.

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.500
As Hammer explains, astrology
facilitates something

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.950
called Narrativism,
which "conveys the idea

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.190
that we tell the stories of our lives,

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:18.180
stories that construct a temporal
unity for our identities,

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.200
and that link our specific life histories

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.450
with purported grand overarching themes."

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:23.830
In this way, Hammer writes,

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.670
it "offers a conceptual framework

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:27.930
for constructing a
narrative unity of life"

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:29.670
and "furnishes a narrative form

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:32.230
within which one's life
history can be understood."

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:33.590
Hammer even says these narratives

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.450
can function as
"therapeutic interventions."

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.390
Though please don't break
up with your therapist

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:38.910
just because you can
blame all your problems

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.510
on Mercury being in retrograde.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:41.920
Linguist Charlotte Linde argues

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:44.300
that narrative is one of
the most powerful ways

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.450
of creating and maintaining
one's personal identity.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.990
Narrativizing can also help
you establish causality

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:51.610
and coherency in your life story.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.770
Didn't get asked to prom?

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.020
Blame pesky Venus.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.211
Didn't get that promotion?

00:11:55.211 --> 00:11:56.190
(beep) You, Mars!

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.550
Essentially, astrology
can help us explain away

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.530
the apparent randomness of human life.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.520
And according to Linde,

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:02.700
it can do that regardless

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.510
of if we fully believe in it or not!

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:05.567
As Munk summarized,

00:12:05.567 --> 00:12:07.300
"In such a disorderly world,

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:08.860
astrology offers a symbolic

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.750
and metaphorical system of imagining

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.100
within a frame of order."

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:13.620
Even if that order is, you know,

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.100
not at all scientifically proven

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.500
and pretty randomly concocted

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.417
by a few savvy 20th century
spiritual entrepreneurs.

00:12:19.417 --> 00:12:20.690
But what do you guys think?

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.670
Is astrology distinctly modern,

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.470
or a lingering remnant
of ancient spirituality?

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.220
Let us know what you
think in the comments.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.970
Big thanks to our patrons
for all your support,

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.840
and be sure to check out our podcasts.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:31.860
Hit that Subscribe button

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.900
with the fury of a vengeful Capricorn,

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:35.670
and don't forget to ring that bell.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:39.208
And as always, thanks for watching, peace.

